<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ceretic of Elmet</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">died c. 616</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ceretic was the last known king of Elmet, a British kingdom in what is now <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-yorkshire">West Yorkshire</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/historia-brittonum">Historia Brittonum</a> says that <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edwin-of-northumbria">Edwin of Northumbria</a> seized Elmet and expelled him, usually dated around 617, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/annales-cambriae">Annales Cambriae</a> record his death about that time. His fall ended the last independent British kingdom east of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pennines">Pennines</a>.</p></div>
